///
/// The prior port collapsed this into a single auto-pick of the
/// shuffle's first card. The shuffle read-count matched C# (both shuffle
/// the whole pool), but the harness drives C#'s choose-a-card screen with
/// its own action RNG, which may land on the 2nd or 3rd option — so the
/// auto-pick desynced the resulting hand. Presenting the real
/// [`ChoiceKind::AddGeneratedFreeToHand`] choice lets the harness pick the
/// same index. The resolver materialises only the chosen id, stamps it
